    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d821">

                <pb facs="0765" n="593" xml:id="pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.6211/413</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-08T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4418. The British Ambassador has received telegram from his Government saying
                    that safe-conduct will be granted for Bernstorff and his party, and that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Frederik VIII</hi> will be examined at Halifax if it is
                    especially desired. Please inform Foreign Office that in the circumstances the
                    Department would be grateful if the British authorities would carry out their
                    examination at Halifax and not at Kirkwall.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
